  "worked_solution": "First, notice that we have $R={R}_{1}\\cup {R}_{2}$, where ${R}_{1}=(0,1)\\times (-1,0)$ and ${R}_{2}=(0,1)\\times (0,1).$ So, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A= & ={\u222c}_{{R}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{\u222c}_{{R}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{{R}_{1}}6x\\,\\text{d}A+{\u222c}_{{R}_{2}}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{{R}_{1}}6x\\,\\text{d}A+{\u222c}_{{R}_{2}}({e}^{x})({e}^{y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =(0-(-1)){\\int }_{0}^{1}6x\\,\\text{d}x+({\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =[3{x}^{2}]_{0}^{1}+[{e}^{x}]_{0}^{1}\\cdot [{e}^{y}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =3+(e-1)^{2} \\\\  & ={e}^{2}-2e+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
